{title: 137 - We Three Kings}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #137 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 137}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Em]We three kings of [B7]Orient [Em]are;
Bearing gifts we [B7]traverse [Em]afar
Field and [D]fountain, [G]moor and mountain,
[Am]Following [Em]yon[B]der [Em]star.
[D]O [D7] [G]star of wonder, [C]star of [G]night,
Star with royal [C]beauty [G]bright,
[Em]Westward [D]lead[G]ing, [C]still [G]pro[D]ceed[G]ing,
Guide us to Thy [C]perfect [G]light.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[Em]O star [B7]of wonder, [Em]star of night,
[B7]Star with [Em]royal beauty bright,
[D]Westward leading, [G]still proceeding,
[Am]Guide [Em]us to [B]Thy [Em]perfect light.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Em]Born a [B7]King on [Em]Bethlehem's plain,
[B7]Gold I bring [Em]to crown Him again,
[D]King forever, [G]ceasing never
[Am]Over [Em]us [B]all [Em]to reign.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Em]Frankincense [B7]to offer [Em]have I;
[B7]Incense owns [Em]a Deity nigh;
[D]Prayer and praising [G]all men raising,
[Am]Worship [Em]Him, [B]God [Em]on high.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Em]Myrrh is [B7]mine; its [Em]bitter perfume
[B7]Breathes a life [Em]of gathering gloom:
[D]Sorrowing, sighing, [G]bleeding, dying,
[Am]Sealed [Em]in [B]the [Em]stonecold tomb.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[Em]Glorious [B7]now behold [Em]Him arise,
[B7]King and [Em]God and sacrifice;
[D]Alleluia, [G]Alleluia!
[Am]Sounds [Em]through the [B]earth [Em]and skies.
{end_of_verse}
